<!-- 3 SERVICES -->
<section class="light" id="services"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">What we build and run</p>
 <h2>Seven window and door marketing services, one connected system</h2>
 <p class="lead">A marketing system with seven parts performs at the level of its weakest one. The <a href="/6-gap-revenue-map/">6-Gap Revenue Map™</a> shows which part is leaking most, and we start there, often on the inquiries you already have.</p>
 <div class="tlax" aria-hidden="true"><span>Marketing that brings the inquiry</span><span>Sales systems that sign it</span></div>
 <ol class="tline">
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="svp1"><span class="tn">01</span><span class="tw">Generate targeted demand</span><span class="th">Google Ads and Local Services Ads</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp1" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb1"><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">01 · Generate targeted demand</p><p>Google Ads and Local Services Ads for window and door companies, built by product and city, filtered against DIY and repair searches, and judged on cost per booked job. Meta ads and retargeting stay in front of homeowners comparing quotes, and direct mail reaches neighborhoods with aging windows. <a class="tl" href="/ppc-for-window-and-door-companies/">PPC for window and door <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 2–4 weeks, in new estimate requests.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp2"><span class="tn">02</span><span class="tw">Build lasting local visibility</span><span class="th">Local SEO and Google Maps</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp2" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb2" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">02 · Build lasting local visibility</p><p>Local SEO for window and door companies: own the map pack in the towns you sell, then the pages behind it: "window replacement [city]," "entry door installation near me," "patio door replacement." <a class="tl" href="/seo-for-window-and-door-companies/">SEO for window and door <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 3–6 months, then compounds for years.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp3"><span class="tn">03</span><span class="tw">Own your lead source</span><span class="th">Exclusive leads you own</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp3" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb3" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">03 · Own your lead source</p><p>Exclusive window and door leads, generated, not bought: homeowners who contacted you and only you, from a marketing engine you keep. No shared queue, no three other companies calling the same house. <a class="tl" href="/window-and-door-lead-generation/">Lead generation <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> as the mix shifts, with close rates in a different class.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp4"><span class="tn">04</span><span class="tw">Turn research into estimates</span><span class="th">A website that books the estimate</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp4" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb4" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">04 · Turn research into estimates</p><p>A window and door website that turns research into estimate requests: pages for each product and city, financing made clear, proof where the decision happens, and one next step.</p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 4–8 weeks, across every channel.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp5"><span class="tn">05</span><span class="tw">Win the comparison</span><span class="th">Reviews and referrals</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp5" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb5" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">05 · Win the comparison</p><p>Reviews and referrals that compound: every customer asked for a review after every install, every review answered, and referrals asked for while the new windows are still the talk of the street. <a class="tl" href="/services/reputation-management-for-contractors/">Reputation <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> 2–3 months, then every month after.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp6"><span class="tn">06</span><span class="tw">Convert the inquiries you get</span><span class="th">Speed to lead and estimate follow-up</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp6" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb6" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">06 · Convert the inquiries you get</p><p>First contact in minutes, the in-home estimate booked and confirmed, the no-show prevented, then every estimate followed up until it's signed or lost. The marketing you already paid for, finally answered. It lifts every channel above at once. <a class="tl" href="/services/lead-to-booked-job/">How it works <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> this week, on inquiries you already have.</p></div></li>
  <li><h3 class="tb"><button type="button" id="svb7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="svp7"><span class="tn">07</span><span class="tw">Connect marketing to signed jobs</span><span class="th">Attribution to the signed job</span></button></h3><div class="tp" id="svp7" role="region" aria-labelledby="svb7" data-closed><p class="tph">How we fix it</p><p class="tpw">07 · Connect marketing to signed jobs</p><p>Every call, form and estimate tagged to its source and followed to sold or lost, so each channel's true cost per signed install decides next month's budget. <a class="tl" href="/attribution/">How we measure it <span class="ar">→</span></a></p><p class="when"><b>When it pays:</b> every month.</p></div></li>
 </ol>
 <p class="tlhint">Tap any step for what it covers.</p>
</div></section>

<!-- 4 MATH: table + calculator -->
<section class="soft" id="math"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">What the marketing gap costs</p>
 <h2>In window and door marketing, the cheapest lead is often your <span class="o">most expensive job.</span></h2>
 <p class="lead">Your marketing report ends at the inquiry. Your business runs on the signed job, and the two can point in opposite directions.</p>
 <table class="cmp rpt">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">The report says</th><th scope="col">What's really happening</th><th scope="col">So you</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
   <tr><th scope="row">"Marketplace leads are your cheapest marketing."</th><td data-l="What's really happening">Each one went to three or four companies at once. About 4% sell.</td><td data-l="So you">Keep paying for the marketing that costs the most per signed job.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">"We need more volume before spring."</th><td data-l="What's really happening">New inquiries wait an hour for a callback. Someone else is already measuring the windows.</td><td data-l="So you">Raise marketing spend, when speed was the problem.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">"Inquiries are up again."</th><td data-l="What's really happening">Estimates get run and go quiet. Signed jobs are flat.</td><td data-l="So you">Buy more marketing, when the kitchen-table close is the leak.</td></tr>
   <tr><th scope="row">"Let's push harder for fall."</th><td data-l="What's really happening">Your install crews are already booked out for weeks.</td><td data-l="So you">Pay for demand you can't install.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
 </table>
 <div class="calc" id="calc">
  <h3>The same $200 lead, two very different jobs</h3>
  <p class="sub">Every marketing vendor sells you cost per lead. Cost per booked job is the number that decides your budget. Change the numbers to yours. Nothing you enter is saved.</p>
  <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Lead type"><button type="button" data-v="4" aria-pressed="false">Shared marketplace lead · 4%</button><button type="button" data-v="11.7" aria-pressed="true">Direct inquiry, your own lead · 11.7%</button></div>
  <div class="cgrid">
   <div class="ins">
    <div><label for="wdCpl">Your cost per lead</label><output id="wdCplOut">$200</output><input type="range" id="wdCpl" min="20" max="600" step="1" value="200"></div>
    <div><label for="wdCr">Your close rate on those leads</label><output id="wdCrOut">11.7%</output><input type="range" id="wdCr" min="1" max="40" step="0.1" value="11.7"></div>
    <div><label for="wdJob">Average job</label><output id="wdJobOut">$7,348</output><input type="range" id="wdJob" min="1000" max="40000" step="1" value="7348"></div>
   </div>
   <div class="res" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="k">True cost per booked job</p>
    <p class="big"><span id="wdCpj">$1,709</span> <small id="wdOne">About 1 in 9 inquiries becomes a job.</small></p>
    <p class="gp" id="wdPct">23% of a $7,348 average job.</p>
    <p class="now" id="wdCmp">The same $200 lead at 4% costs $5,000 per job, 68% of the ticket.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <details class="how"><summary>Sources and how it's calculated</summary><p>Cost per booked job = cost per lead ÷ close rate: $200 ÷ 4% = $5,000, and $200 ÷ 11.7% = $1,709. Average doors-and-windows search-ad lead $200.34 (LocaliQ, 2025). Average window replacement job $7,348 (Angi, updated Oct 2026, 17,857 projects). Close rates by source come from the founder's own lead ledger at one dealership (not a window and door company), same team and same months: shared marketplace leads 3.9–4.1%, direct inquiries 11.6–11.8%. Illustration, not a client result.</p></details>
 </div>
 <p class="midcta"><a class="btn" href="https://calendly.com/andrew-andrewryanmarketing/gap-review?utm_source=arm-site&amp;utm_medium=cta&amp;utm_campaign=site&amp;utm_content=wd-mid">Let's talk about your marketing&nbsp;<span class="ar">→</span></a><span>Bring your real numbers. We'll run them with you.</span></p>
</div></section>

<!-- 5 WHERE JOBS ARE WON OR LOST + GROWTH PATHS -->
<section class="light" id="leaks"><div class="in">
 <p class="eb">Where the job is won or lost</p>
 <h2>Most agencies report the first step. The job is decided in the last three.</h2>
 <p class="lead">A homeowner replaces windows once every 15 to 40 years, compares several companies, and decides at the kitchen table. A marketing report that ends at the form fill sees none of that. We follow it to the signed install.</p>
 <ol class="path">
  <li><span class="st">1 · The search</span><b>Found isn't chosen</b><h3>"Window replacement near me"</h3><p>Your ad, map listing or page has to win the click, then the inquiry: a form or a call.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">2 · The inquiry</span><b>Reached in 5 minutes</b><h3>Before another company calls back</h3><p>The homeowner asked three companies. The first one to reach them usually gets the estimate.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">3 · The estimate</span><b>Quoted isn't signed</b><h3>Measured, priced, financed</h3><p>The kitchen-table visit, the financing question and the follow-up decide it. Most agencies never see this step.</p></li>
  <li><span class="st">4 · The install</span><b>The only number that pays&nbsp;you</b><h3>Signed and installed</h3><p>Crew capacity decides how much demand you can use, so marketing never outruns what your crews can install.</p></li>
 </ol>
 <h3 class="h3x">Where should your next million in installs come from?</h3>
 <div class="paths3">
  <div><p class="tag">Own your home market</p><h4>You're known in town. The bigger brand still gets the first call.</h4><p>Take the map pack, the reviews and the estimate path in the towns you already serve.</p><a class="tl" href="/seo-for-window-and-door-companies/">See what it takes <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
  <div><p class="tag">Open the next market</p><h4>New town, no reviews, no referrals.</h4><p>See the cost per installed job there before you hire a crew or sign a lease.</p><a class="tl" href="/contractor-growth-marketing/">Model the next market <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
  <div><p class="tag">Close more of what you run</p><h4>The estimates get run, but too few sign.</h4><p>Fix the callback, the set and the close before you buy more demand.</p><a class="tl" href="/services/lead-to-booked-job/">Fix the second funnel <span class="ar">→</span></a></div>
 </div>
</div></section>

